D069 (founder request, 2026-11-13; F6; wiki/decisions/D069-openai-ads-measurement.md): the order remembers which ChatGPT
ad click brought the buyer. One import and the `fb_attrib:` line: `withOpenAiAttrib(readFbAttrib(request), request)` merges
`oai_oppref` and `oai_obref`, read from the request's cookies and validated, into the SAME `fb_attrib` JSONB Meta's
attribution already lives in. There is NO new column and NO migration (a migration is applied by hand, and code that
inserted a new column ahead of it would answer every pre-order with a 500); Meta's reader picks only its own four keys.
`fb_attrib` stays null only when both are empty. The amount, the tier, the validation, the order of operations, the rate
limit, the Razorpay call and every response are unchanged.

